14
00:01:00,806 --> 00:01:04,100
Shares for growth. Core for a broader range.

15
00:01:04,361 --> 00:01:08,077
Active for staged conversions. Cash for the next opportunity.

16
00:01:09,184 --> 00:01:13,410
Explore how the strategy behaves over one to five years.

17
00:01:13,955 --> 00:01:19,579
For this example, let’s choose three years, with rallies and pullbacks.

18
00:01:20,821 --> 00:01:24,883
As the price rises, Active turns some shares into cash.

19
00:01:25,145 --> 00:01:28,855
When it pulls back, available cash can rebuild inventory.

20
00:01:29,115 --> 00:01:32,154
As it recovers, the strategy redeploys.

21
00:01:32,415 --> 00:01:37,815
Shares, cash, and liquidity keep changing—while in-range trades earn fees.

22
00:01:38,914 --> 00:01:44,476
Daily research checks new disclosures, news, and operating data against the model.

23
00:01:44,866 --> 00:01:48,624
Sources, assumptions, and decisions stay traceable.

24
00:01:49,015 --> 00:01:52,010
Material changes prompt a valuation review.

25
00:01:53,247 --> 00:01:58,144
Now suppose stronger growth and better margins support a higher valuation.

26
00:01:58,406 --> 00:02:02,645
At year two, review the valuation and move Core higher.

27
